WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
We have undertaken a historic effort to massively

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.680
reduce job-crushing regulations.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.880
Sounded good to me,

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.340
but the media says Trump is wrecking America.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.520
This is a very big deal.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.860
The Environmental Protection Agency

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.580
just rolled back Obama-era climate rules.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.200
He singlehandedly led the world down a dark path.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.230
His proposal is literally insane.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.140
We’re told his deregulation

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.740
is an attack on the environment,

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.940
that workers health, safety, and pay are casualties,

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.770
and even that Trump is trying to kill us.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.200
Now Trump has cut regulations

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.600
This is where we were in 1960.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.120
He promised to shrink the regulation rulebook

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.200
back to the size it was 58 years ago.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.560
We will have a great regulatory climate.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.080
One. Two. three.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.579
[applause]

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:48.620
The day he got elected,

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.390
you saw the stock markets swing up.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.140
Grover Norquist runs a group that

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.150
fights for lower taxes and fewer rules.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.900
Trump sent a message to business:

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.150
we're not going to crush you, and that's caused growth.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.260
That was the beginning of a recovery.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.920
In the 48 hours since Donald Trump

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.360
was elected to the Oval Office,

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.680
the stock market has rallied, reaching new heights.

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:12.840
And the Trump administration has repealed lots of rules,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.060
for example…

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.000
Waters of the United States.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.440
We've got to protect waters of the United States.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.080
Sounds good.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.000
They were including little trickles,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.220
the kind of ponds that spring up

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.040
when it rains a lot one night,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.220
and then it goes away the next day.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:27.549
They were using it as land control.

00:01:27.549 --> 00:01:29.460
Land control can crush people.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.070
Jill and Jack Barron were encouraged by Idaho officials

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.860
to clear a drainage ditch,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.460
but when they did that,

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.250
federal officials went after them,

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.060
fining them thousands of dollars.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.969
37,500 a day

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:45.940
Until the Barrons had to sell their home

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.369
and move into this trailer

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:50.440
But now thanks to deregulation,

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.350
they can use their land again. Good.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.600
But other repealed rules sound important.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.160
The names for all these regulations

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.680
are written by the regulators.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.940
They're advertisements for themselves

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.580
But unlike many advertisers,

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.180
regulators don’t list the side effects

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.000
Some people have had changes in behavior,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.600
hostility, agitation

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.060
May cause unemployment, may reduce wages,

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:14.760
may raise the cost of energy,

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.100
may make your car not drivable.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.040
[CAR NOISE]

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.760
Well, its drivable, but smaller because the Obama rules

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.040
would have forced car makers

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.960
to nearly double gas mileage,

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.180
and more people are killed in smaller cars

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.200
Should the government tell you what kind of car to buy?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.940
Should they? And that's what the regulation does.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.200
Now California regulators have made a deal

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.360
with 4 automakers to keep the Obama rules,

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.500
in effect telling Californians,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.440
some cars you cannot have.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.160
Net neutrality for everyone

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.900
Trump’s FCC also ended “net neutrality” rules.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.980
They were going to turn the internet,

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.260
which is a free, largely free, and open operation

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.420
into a government regulated utility monopoly

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.680
When Trump repealed that,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.000
people said he was

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Handing the keys to the internet over to a

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.020
handful of multi-billion-dollar corporations

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.780
Bad things were going to happen.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.260
They were going to charge you to do this, that

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.260
and the other thing.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.280
The companies would send your emails slower

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.480
than somebody else's.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.280
None of that's happened.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.600
None of it. None of it. None of it.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.420
The 2 for $5 mix and match deal

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.440
from McDonald’s is back.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.920
Many regulations were repealed

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.500
that few people know about.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.820
One would’ve treated franchise companies

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.580
like McDonald’s as one single business.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.080
Why? The trial lawyers want to be able

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.200
to sue all of McDonald’s,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.060
not just the local McDonald’s,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.960
if they spill coffee on themselves.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.340
And the labor unions wanted to unionize

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.920
all of McDonald’s, not just the one store.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.160
That would have been a disaster.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.300
That was ended.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.380
Deregulation. It’s when we remove those bad rules

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:53.500
so that corporations can maximize their profits. Ha ha!

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.740
People think Trump is destroying the workplace

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.220
and the environment.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.660
If you get your news from late night comedy shows,

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.940
you think that deregulation is bad

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.580
for the economy and bad for the environment.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.240
In point of fact it's good for the environment,

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.580
it's good for jobs,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.700
it's good for people having more wealth.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.260
But we want the air to be cleaner.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.500
The air is getting cleaner. It's dramatically cleaner.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.200
It is. Mostly because of EPA rules

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.840
passed decades ago...

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.480
and every time someone replaces

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.220
an old car with a new one the air gets a little cleaner.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.620
Now climate change and whether we can do anything

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.340
about that is a separate debate,

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.860
but when it comes to clean air Trump’s

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:36.400
undoing of Obama’s ever-stricter standards

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.600
just returns us to the rules in effect

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.900
during the Clinton and Bush years.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.520
Were you coughing then?

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.300
No, but the media won’t tell you that.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.080
President Trump has liberated American factories

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.980
from the scourge of pollution rules.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:52.880
[coughs]

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.000
Lost in the coughing is the unfortunate fact

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.180
that Trump is adding regulations too!

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.340
It’s all about “made in America”

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.080
Now government agencies have to buy

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.780
more American made stuff.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.600
That sounds like a good idea,

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.540
but it's a dumb idea and I wish he hadn't done it.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.280
That is not deregulation. That is regulation.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.600
Stocks tumbling today

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.800
Markets that rose when he was elected

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.980
have dropped as Trump's tariffs

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.380
punish&nbsp;American companies that buy steel

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.440
and consumers who want things like

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.820
washing machines and solar panels.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:23.940
There is a challenge.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.560
Trump is a protectionist in many ways.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.340
And then I can always do much more

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.360
or I can do less,

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.180
depending on what happens with respect to a deal

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.460
and tariffs are taxes and regulations on the border,

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.240
are regulations on consumers,

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.640
and frankly it hasn’t cost our consumers anything.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.560
It costs China.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.020
The good news is,

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.800
the vast majority of the regulatory acts

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.440
by a factor of many have been deregulatory

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.220
and they have been tremendously helpful

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.560
And yet with all this publicity about Trump deregulating,

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.560
he hasn't done that much.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.080
He's done a great deal more than anybody

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.560
in recent history, maybe even more than Reagan did.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:05.920
We have cut 22 regulations

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.400
for every one new regulation.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.520
Think of that one

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.920
He exaggerates, as usual.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.560
The real number is about 5 repealed

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.100
for every new one passed.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.940
But that’s still pretty good.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.720
He’s loosened all these rules.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.600
It’s good whenever excessive regulations are cut.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.480
Regulations are like taxes.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.880
They take choices away from ...

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:26.860
the government takes your money.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:27.880
You don't get to decide what to do.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.600
You have to go work more hours,

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:30.800
spend less time with your family,

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.100
less time of things you want to do.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:32.980
They take your time.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:33.940
[Thud]

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.260
They cost us money,

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.500
[Thud]

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.360
deprive us of opportunities,

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.760
[Thud]

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.200
they take our freedom.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.260
[Thud]

